# Player_JoinOrSpawn: the spawn refused for a full object pool (ruling 5, 2), at its first call (a
# player slot object, a6+$1E = its record): the record in play (+$25 bit 0), g_ObjPoolFree = 0
# (140 blocks at scene init, every Obj_New / ObjPool_Alloc* takes one), so the 3-block allocation
# fails and the slot waits to retry next frame. A busy screen can hold every block when a player
# respawns (after a lost life) or joins.

case pool_full
b [a6 + $1E] + $25 = 1
b $FFFFF4B0 = 0
